-- Plan — an offer expressed as a single expression: context in, terms
-- out. The `terms` field holds JSON Logic producing Term[]; empty
-- array = offer doesn't apply.
--
-- Static rows: none. Identity + the per-field widget hint are lifted from
-- the directives below (FM-retire-E1 Step 2 + Step 5); the auto-register
-- loop in system-entities.ts registers the entity. The pre-flip
-- `defineSystemEntity` (with its `fieldUi.terms` widget overlay) is GONE.
--   - `@widget "terms" "expression"` — the editor mounts the expression
--     editor for `terms`.
--   - `@helpText "terms" "JSON Logic → Term[]"` — the body returns Term[].
--
-- TODO: the `terms` field's `{}` (empty record) shape is preserved
-- bug-compatibly from the pre-3d TS literal. The real schema for
-- terms (JSON Logic returning Term[]) is out of scope for this phase
-- and lands when the Plan entity gets a fully-typed body — Term ADT
-- + return-type assertion.

@entity
@codeName "plan"
@label "Plan"
@description "An offer — one expression: context in, terms out"
@icon "receipt"
@widget "terms" "expression"
@helpText "terms" "JSON Logic → Term[]"
Plan = Plan slug: String name: String terms: {}
